ConverterDomTest
├── convertPricesInDocument
│   ├── it converts the whole page
│   ├── it gives every price on the page one decimal shape
│   ├── it starts a fresh scale for each page it is given
│   ├── given conversion is switched off
│   │   └── it does nothing
│   ├── given the rates cannot be used
│   │   └── it does nothing
│   └── given there is no body
│       └── it does nothing
├── convertPricesInNode
│   ├── it wraps converted prices in marked spans with an accurate tooltip
│   ├── it reverts precisely, restoring the original text
│   ├── given append mode
│   │   └── it keeps the original price visible
│   ├── given a price inside a button
│   │   └── it never rewrites it
│   ├── given a price split across inline child nodes
│   │   └── it converts it
│   ├── given a child also holds a price
│   │   └── it converts a parent's direct text too
│   ├── given conversion is switched off
│   │   └── it does nothing
│   ├── given rates that cannot be used
│   │   └── it refuses to convert with empty or stale rates
│   ├── given no price converts
│   │   └── it leaves the element alone
│   ├── given the same price twice in one element
│   │   └── it converts both from one replacement
│   ├── given a longer price contains a shorter one
│   │   └── it replaces the longer one
│   ├── given two different prices in one text node
│   │   ├── it replaces them in the order they appear
│   │   └── it replaces the longer of two that start together
│   ├── given the same price written twice in one text node
│   │   └── it converts both from one replacement
│   ├── given a price only its container's whole text spells out
│   │   ├── it replaces the container
│   │   └── given the container also holds other text
│   │       └── it is left alone
│   ├── given a converted container gains other content
│   │   └── the new content IS converted
│   ├── given a converted span gains other content
│   │   └── the new content is not converted inside it
│   ├── given one of our spans is left inside an element being converted
│   │   └── its text is not replaced again
│   ├── given text inside a contenteditable region
│   │   ├── it is left alone
│   │   └── given it sits under a convertible element
│   │       └── it is still left alone
│   ├── given text inside a skipped tag
│   │   ├── it is left alone
│   │   └── given it sits under a convertible element
│   │       └── it is still left alone
│   └── given text inside a button
│       ├── it is left alone
│       └── given it sits under a convertible element
│           └── it is still left alone
│   ├── given its own output
│   │   ├── it never re-processes it
│   │   ├── given a second pass over an already-converted element
│   │   │   └── it is skipped
│   │   ├── given the element itself is marked converted
│   │   │   └── it is skipped
│   │   └── given a second pass over one of our own spans
│   │       └── it is skipped
│   ├── given the settings carry no anchors at all
│   │   └── it converts without a ratio line
│   └── given script or style content
│       └── it skips it
├── anchors turn a price into a quantity
│   ├── it adds a ratio line to the tooltip
│   └── given no anchors are set
│       └── it leaves the tooltip alone
├── weaning withdraws the fiat crutch
│   ├── given weaning is switched off entirely
│   │   └── it keeps the original whatever the start date says
│   ├── given weaning has reached the hidden stage
│   │   └── it drops the original from the tooltip
│   └── given weaning is on but has not reached that stage
│       └── it keeps the original
├── the held-rate disclosure states its age
│   ├── it signs a gap above spot positive
│   ├── given the peg was taken exactly an hour ago
│   │   └── it says one hour, not just now
│   ├── given the peg was taken minutes ago
│   │   └── it says just now
│   ├── given the peg was taken hours ago
│   │   └── it says how many hours
│   ├── given the peg was taken a day ago
│   │   └── it says one day
│   ├── given the peg was taken several days ago
│   │   └── it says how many days
│   └── given spot has fallen below the peg
│       └── it signs the gap negative
├── copying a converted price yields the fiat
│   ├── it swaps ZEC back to the original in clipboard text
│   ├── it stops the browser writing the ZEC text over the top
│   ├── it catches the copy before the page can
│   ├── it stops swapping once the handler is removed
│   └── given the selection is empty
│       └── it leaves the clipboard alone
│   ├── given a selection with no converted price
│   │   └── it leaves the selection alone
│   ├── given nothing is selected
│   │   └── it leaves the clipboard alone
│   └── given a span the page created
│       └── it leaves it alone
├── reverting
│   ├── it puts the original text back in place
│   ├── it clears the marker so the element can convert again
│   ├── it clears the marker on a partly converted element too
│   ├── given a span the page created
│   │   └── it is left alone
│   ├── given a container that had no title before
│   │   └── the title is removed rather than emptied
│   └── given a container that had its own title
│       └── the title is put back
├── hide-fiat mode
│   ├── it drops the original from the tooltip but keeps the ratio
│   └── it still gives the fiat back on copy — thinking in ZEC, not unable to pay
├── the held rate reaches the page
│   ├── it converts at the held rate, not spot
│   ├── it always discloses the gap from spot, with no fiat figure
│   └── given the user asked for spot
│       └── it falls back to spot
└── a site adapter that replaces the whole container
    ├── it replaces a bol.com price container
    ├── it leaves an accessible copy behind
    ├── it hides that copy from sight
    ├── it separates two prices in one container
    ├── it clears the original markup rather than appending to it
    ├── it keeps the untrimmed original out of the tooltip
    └── given the container had a title of its own
        └── it puts that title back on revert
